{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BTUkMJ3cMQtYiHFHYycSjJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils derives formal specs from C source code of classic Unix utilities, generates Go implementations from those specs using an AI agent, and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries via differential testing. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) with `cmd/` for utility implementations, `pkg/testutils/` for differential testing, `pkg/sys/` for platform syscall wrappers, `pkg/format/` for shared formatting, `docs/` for specifications, and `magefiles/` for build targets.\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists for pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/cat, cmd/du, cmd/ls, cmd/sponge, cmd/wc, and cmd/version. All spec-complete utilities have implementations. The remaining releases (rel02.0: true/false/yes/basename/dirname, rel02.1: tee, rel02.2: head/seq) have specstatus: pending, blocking code generation.\n\n**Current release**: rel02.0 (Batch 2 — trivial utilities) is the earliest incomplete release, but all five use cases are blocked on human-authored specifications. Preceding releases (00.0, 01.1, 01.2, 01.3, 03.0, 04.0) have implementations in source_code.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nAll spec-complete releases have code in source_code. rel02.0 is blocked on pending specs (human-authored per DD5). The only actionable work anchored to known PRD requirement IDs is gap-filling: `pkg/sys/terminal.go` implements prd002-sys R1.1 and R1.2 but has no corresponding test file (fileinfo_test.go exists but terminal_test.go does not). Adding it completes test coverage for rel00.0-uc003-sys.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd002-sys R1.1, R1.2 -- Add TerminalWidth unit tests\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml (R1.1 terminal width query, R1.2 implementation via golang.org/x/sys/unix)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (TerminalWidth implementation being tested)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo_test.go (test patterns -- build tags, package name, t.Parallel, error assertions)\n      - pkg/format/color_test.go (os.Pipe pattern for non-terminal FD testing)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for TerminalWidth covering non-terminal FD error paths and safe handling\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test that TerminalWidth returns a non-nil error when passed the read end of an os.Pipe file descriptor, verifying non-terminal FDs are correctly rejected (prd002-sys R1.1)\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test that TerminalWidth returns a non-nil error when passed the write end of an os.Pipe file descriptor, exercising a second non-terminal FD (prd002-sys R1.1)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test that TerminalWidth returns a non-nil error when passed a regular file descriptor opened via os.CreateTemp, confirming error handling for file-backed FDs (prd002-sys R1.1)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test that TerminalWidth does not panic for any valid non-terminal file descriptor; the function must return an error cleanly without crashing (prd002-sys R1.1)\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Test file uses package sys_test (external test package) and //go:build darwin || linux build tag, matching the existing fileinfo_test.go conventions (prd002-sys R1.2)\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use os.Pipe() to create non-terminal file descriptors for negative testing, following the same pattern used in pkg/format/color_test.go TestColorEnabled_Pipe\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use //go:build darwin || linux build tag to match terminal.go and fileinfo_test.go platform constraints\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Do not assert TerminalWidth succeeds on os.Stdout or os.Stderr; test runners pipe these descriptors, making TTY detection environment-dependent and non-deterministic\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/sys/terminal_test.go exists, compiles, and passes go vet\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"All tests pass via go test ./pkg/sys/...\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Test file begins with //go:build darwin || linux build tag\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Test file is in package sys_test (external test package)\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Every test function calls t.Parallel()\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Pipe and regular file tests verify TerminalWidth returns a non-nil error\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"Copyright header and SPDX license identifier match project convention (see fileinfo_test.go lines 1-2)\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":99245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"480e051b-de75-4785-b118-4f2ea1388be4","uuid":"1bac8536-962d-438a-a7e7-cf39d758e042"}
